    "Promise/sign check: yes means Phi>=delta; no means abs(Phi)<=delta/2. A large negative Phi is off-promise. A Phi^2 decoder can accept such an input; this is permitted only because total-function verification rejects invalid address certificates with its proved bounded-error guarantee. This is a textual mathematical requirement, not a numerical test.",
